1
00:00:00,536 --> 00:00:02,469
Every group trip has a treasurer.

2
00:00:02,754 --> 00:00:04,455
They put the cabin on their own card,

3
00:00:04,543 --> 00:00:06,269
chase eight friends for their share,

4
00:00:06,357 --> 00:00:07,457
pay the boat rental,

5
00:00:07,619 --> 00:00:09,126
and work out what the friend who dropped

6
00:00:09,126 --> 00:00:10,068
out gets back.

7
00:00:11,424 --> 00:00:13,774
Purser is an agent that does that job

8
00:00:13,777 --> 00:00:15,821
through PayPal. The difference:

9
00:00:16,069 --> 00:00:17,588
it can only do what the ledger says

10
00:00:17,588 --> 00:00:18,198
is owed.

11
00:00:19,516 --> 00:00:20,950
You describe the trip the way you would

12
00:00:20,950 --> 00:00:21,866
in the group chat.

13
00:00:22,151 --> 00:00:23,938
Gemini reads it into a ledger:

14
00:00:24,344 --> 00:00:26,281
who is coming, who already paid for

15
00:00:26,281 --> 00:00:28,704
what, the boat company still to be paid,

16
00:00:29,001 --> 00:00:31,636
and the sponsor. Every name it returns

17
00:00:31,636 --> 00:00:33,055
has to appear in the brief.

18
00:00:36,516 --> 00:00:37,874
Then the treasurer runs,

19
00:00:37,987 --> 00:00:40,459
live, on the PayPal sandbox,

20
00:00:40,487 --> 00:00:42,236
through the PayPal Agent Toolkit.

21
00:00:42,509 --> 00:00:44,237
One order per person for their exact

22
00:00:44,237 --> 00:00:46,587
share, an invoice to the sponsor,

23
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:48,682
sent. Reimbursements wait,

24
00:00:48,795 --> 00:00:51,047
because the pot is still empty.

25
00:00:54,528 --> 00:00:56,180
Priya opens her personal link,

26
00:00:56,452 --> 00:00:58,533
sees exactly what she is paying for,

27
00:00:58,830 --> 00:01:01,109
and goes straight to PayPal's own sandbox

28
00:01:01,109 --> 00:01:01,756
checkout.

29
00:01:03,504 --> 00:01:05,021
In the no-keys demo mode,

30
00:01:05,256 --> 00:01:07,168
a labelled checkout simulator plays

31
00:01:07,168 --> 00:01:09,800
PayPal's part. Priya approves,

32
00:01:09,913 --> 00:01:12,484
the payment is captured exactly once,

33
00:01:12,719 --> 00:01:14,359
and when Sam pays from his phone,

34
00:01:14,545 --> 00:01:16,687
the organizer's ledger updates live.

35
00:01:18,516 --> 00:01:20,465
Every money move is checked in plain

36
00:01:20,465 --> 00:01:22,508
code before it reaches PayPal.

37
00:01:22,793 --> 00:01:25,352
Here a rogue model tries to pay a stranger,

38
00:01:25,612 --> 00:01:26,810
overcharge Priya,

39
00:01:27,094 --> 00:01:28,992
and pay out money that has not arrived.

40
00:01:29,251 --> 00:01:30,743
All three are denied,

41
00:01:31,065 --> 00:01:32,693
and the reason goes back to the model

42
00:01:32,781 --> 00:01:34,274
so it can correct itself.

43
00:01:38,516 --> 00:01:39,641
Once the money is in,

44
00:01:39,742 --> 00:01:42,205
Jonah's groceries are paid back automatically

45
00:01:42,205 --> 00:01:43,612
with PayPal Payouts.

46
00:01:43,871 --> 00:01:45,930
Maya's cabin reimbursement is above

47
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:48,330
the limit, so it waits for one click.

48
00:01:51,516 --> 00:01:52,580
Kofi can't make it.

49
00:01:52,864 --> 00:01:54,592
He keeps his share of the non-refundable

50
00:01:54,592 --> 00:01:57,215
cabin, the rest is refunded on the payment

51
00:01:57,215 --> 00:01:59,482
he made, and everyone else is asked

52
00:01:59,482 --> 00:02:00,374
for the difference,

53
00:02:00,450 --> 00:02:01,220
to the cent.

54
00:02:04,516 --> 00:02:07,160
Ask the ledger anything in plain English.

55
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:10,261
Every PayPal object and every decision

56
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:11,069
is on the record.

57
00:02:15,516 --> 00:02:17,612
Purser. The treasurer you can trust

58
00:02:17,612 --> 00:02:18,455
with the trip money.

